A||N||9||turbo86se||sounds like someone learned a lesson...||||12||
Z||000000||turbo86se||01-28-2000||11:39 PM||||<BR>well, on my way home from work and school tonight, I stopped at a local BP to pick up a 6-pack of beer. As soon as I got out the door of the BP (I guess I looked ticked off b/c Hingis lost), I hear a high-pitched, almost mouse like engine rev. I look over, and next to my innnocent looking yellow 88 coupe, some ricer with a pearl blue Civic with funky white stripes, slammed suspension, and of course, chrome wheels is parked right next to me. As I got to my door to insert the key, all I could hear was "Fiero" or something snied like that from the driver. Before I could even turn around, I clearly heard the passenger say: "don't mess with the nice Fieros, you never know what's in them!" I just started laughing, and the ricer turned off his engine! We're getting some respect guys and gals!!!!||||reg||12
Z||000001||fiero56||01-29-2000||01:31 AM||||We may be getting some respect now, but not from all. I had a guy in a mid '90s thunderbird go out of his way to try and run me off the road.<BR>I got the bas...ds plate#, if I see that car unatended in a parking lot here in Centerville, well I don't carry a toolbox full of heavy tools just for fixing <B>my</B> car. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||WKDFIRO||01-29-2000||04:11 AM||||The looks that I get are "heh, a Fiero." Right up to the point where I actually start'er up. The loping cam and free exhaust has raised its share of eyebrows.<P>Let'em think its just a Fiero....||||reg||6
Z||000003||batboy||01-29-2000||09:56 AM||||Last September, I had a muffler hanger break loose, so I wheeled into a small town auto repair and muffler shop. The two good ol' boys said sure no problem. One of the guys fired up the Batmobile to pull it onto the rack just as the other one was telling me that he used to own a Fiero once. The V8 roared to life and bubbled noisily at idle. The guy telling me about his old Fiero about dropped his jaw to the ground. He whirled around with wide open eyes and said in amazement, "What's in that sucker!!!" The other guy finished parking it, turned it off, and climbed out saying, "That sounds like a small block!?!" I just grinned like an idiot and popped the decklid for them. They ended charging me just for the hanger (no labor) but I had to B.S. with them for an hour. Both of them were into drag racing. They showed me their "shop" sponsored rail dragster with a 510 racing Chevy big block. Awesome!||||reg||1
Z||000004||turbo86se||01-29-2000||11:27 AM||||batboy, did you get my email last night? I sent a pic of my turbo V6 engine! It's a sweet pic, if you look close enough, you can see the Jet Hot coated back manifold. <BR>A long time ago, I was talking to an ex at a hotel (she was a lifeguard), don't get any funny ideas   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">, and on the highway, I heard this loud scraping noise. I turned over, and I saw a black Fiero, with the entire exhaust dragging on the ground. Cat convertor, muffler, everything with sparks flying everywhere! I shook my head in disblief, my ex laughed and laughed. At this point, I had just bought my first Fiero, didn't know anything about the clubs or Fiero-only stores, and my 85 2m4 was still sitting in my garage going on three months getting it's own new exhaust (flowmaster, and small cat., which sounded awesome!).<BR>I didn't know what to think! My old roommate couldn't wait to get in it! He races cars for Skip Barber, and always talks highly of Fieros, and most of the racers I talked to. Like he said, the Fiero will handle better with a little upgrades than my Miata no matter what I do to it! I agree, man I keep going on and on, I guess I need my medication!  I'm starting to get the shakes!!!<p>[This message has been edited by turbo86se (edited 01-29-2000).]||||reg||10
